<item><title>Nigeria&apos;s central bank to decide on interest rates on November 23</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-central-bank-to-decide-on-interest-rates-on-212bd1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-central-bank-to-decide-on-interest-rates-on-212bd1/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>The Monetary Policy Committee meets on November 23 and 24 to set the Monetary Policy Rate, now 23% after a cut from 26.5% in September.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:08:30 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-central-bank-to-decide-on-interest-rates-on-212bd1/share.jpg" length="42872" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-central-bank-to-decide-on-interest-rates-on-212bd1/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>PCN denies shielding Kano drug dealers, says it sealed 1,631 outlets</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/pcn-denies-shielding-kano-drug-dealers-says-it-sealed-1-631-bef26e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/pcn-denies-shielding-kano-drug-dealers-says-it-sealed-1-631-bef26e/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>The Pharmacy Council of Nigeria says it sealed 1,631 pharmaceutical premises in Kano State this year and has inspected 2,304 drug outlets.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:25:59 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" length="32450" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Nigeria secures $3m deal for 1,000 tomato greenhouses</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-secures-3m-deal-for-1-000-tomato-greenhouses-d12d54/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-secures-3m-deal-for-1-000-tomato-greenhouses-d12d54/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>The agreement, signed at COP31 in Türkiye, is meant to bring private money into climate-smart tomato farming in Kano State.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:53:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" length="32450" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>IFAD, AFD sign deal for rural transformation in Nigeria</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/ifad-afd-sign-deal-for-rural-transformation-in-nigeria-e5489e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/ifad-afd-sign-deal-for-rural-transformation-in-nigeria-e5489e/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>The co-financing agreement backs the Value Chain Programme in Northern Nigeria, which is designed to cut poverty and improve nutrition in rural areas.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:39:05 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" length="32450" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
